Hell or High Water is a 2016 American neo-Western crime drama film
directed by David Mackenzie and written by Taylor Sheridan.

11
00:53:25,714 --> 00:53:31,714
It follows two brothers (Chris Pine and Ben Foster) who carry out a series of bank robberies to save their
family ranch, while being pursued by two Texas Rangers (Jeff Bridges and Gil Birmingham).

12
00:58:17,142 --> 00:58:23,142
It was the final film produced by OddLot
Entertainment before its dissolution in 2015.

13
01:03:08,571 --> 01:03:14,571
Hell or High Water premiered at the Un Certain Regard section of the Cannes Film Festival on May
16, 2016, and was theatrically released in the United States on August 12, 2016.

14
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
It received critical acclaim, particularly for Pine, Foster, and
Bridges' performances, Sheridan's screenplay, and the editing.

15
01:12:51,428 --> 01:12:57,428
It grossed $37.9 million on a $12 million budget.

16
01:17:42,857 --> 01:17:48,857
The American Film Institute selected it as one of its 10 movies of the year, and it was nominated for numerous awards, including
four Oscar nominations: Best Picture, Best Supporting Actor (Bridges), Best Original Screenplay, and Best Editing.

17
01:22:34,285 --> 01:22:40,285
The film is the second installment of writer Taylor Sheridan's American
Frontier Trilogy, along with Sicario and Wind River.

18
01:27:25,714 --> 01:27:31,714
In 2022, it was reported that SK Global is developing a drama
series based on the film for the Fox network.

19
01:32:17,142 --> 01:32:23,142
The film explores themes of brother, texas, bank robber, road trip, gun battle.

20
